Subject: [PATCH] fix(tests): await host-loop lease import during retirement
 reset [daveey]

CI run 44753359633 job 136347244094 preserved the actual first-attempt
traceback: websocket client-kind assertions all passed, but teardown read
host_loop_lease from sys.modules before its background import initialized
_RETIRE_MU. sys.modules publication is not import completion.

Move reset into a small test helper and use import_module to synchronize
with the import lock only if the module has already been used. Preserve
the retirement mutex, clearing semantics and all real websocket assertions.

Proof: an Event-gated real import reproduces the exact AttributeError
with the former direct lookup and passes with synchronization. Verify
unused modules remain unimported, clearing owns the mutex, and the autouse
fixture calls the helper only during teardown. Client-kind=None mutation
fails both agent variants and renderer assertions (3 failures). Restored
4-file focused suite: 30 passed, HERMES_TEST_FILE_RETRIES=0. Historical
merge f0cfeb3f91ecce5019e26719ab00c4f913f1fd90 and current main both pass
ordinary whole-file (4) and focused (2) runs; natural recurrence was not
needed for the controlled import-race proof. Full scripts/check: 21 ok.
